return best;`,type:"fixed"}],bank:["cur = Math.max(a[i], cur + a[i]);","cur = cur + a[i];","cur = Math.max(cur, a[i]);","cur = Math.min(a[i], cur + a[i]);"],correctFill:{g1:"cur = Math.max(a[i], cur + a[i]);"},explanation:"At each element the decision is exactly two-way: extend the run you are on, or abandon it and start fresh at a[i]. Taking the larger is what discards a prefix that has gone negative. Plain cur + a[i] can never restart and sinks with the negatives; max(cur, a[i]) forgets the running sum entirely; and min inverts the whole problem.",hint:"The running sum has gone negative. Is it still worth carrying into the next element?"}],38:[{type:"pair",prompt:"Match pattern to problem",pairs:[{id:1,left:"Sliding window",right:"Max subarray of size k"},{id:2,left:"Two pointer",right:"Pair sum sorted"},{id:3,left:"BFS",right:"Shortest path unweighted"},{id:4,left:"DP",right:"Min coins for amount"}],explanation:'Pattern recognition is the interview meta-skill: "contiguous" points to a window, "sorted + pair" to two pointers, "fewest steps" to BFS, "min/max over choices" to DP. The keywords in a problem statement are the pattern announcing itself.'},{type:"realworld",prompt:"Problem-solving strategy?",scenario:"🎯 You get a hard problem in an interview.",options:[{code:`// 1. Brute force first
